# Comments must be on their own line: loadEnvFile() in server.js does not
# strip a trailing "# ...", so it would become part of the value.
#
# Required. Locally it is the only credential; a hosted server also needs the
# Supabase values below.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional: Google Docs write-back (server/README.md). As of 67120d1
# server/docs-bridge/Code.gs is a one-line placeholder, not the script.
GOOGLE_DOCS_BRIDGE_URL=
# Optional: pair with the token in Code.gs.
TRACELY_BRIDGE_TOKEN=

# ── accounts, plans and billing (hosted deployments; BILLING.md) ─────────────
# SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_ANON_KEY switch enforcement AND the spend cap on;
# absent, nothing is metered or clamped (right on a laptop, ruinous on a
# public box). The live project is https://sxifbtelrtbsgnnwnmdf.supabase.co
# (epafyygdvvkgpdkbevqi is deleted); the anon key is public by design, the
# same one extension/background.js ships.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Only the Stripe webhook uses these, to write plans. Never send the service
# role key to a client.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STRIPE_PRICE_STUDENT=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
# Pins CORS to one extension id. Read once at BOOT: restart after changing it.
# TRACELY_EXTENSION_ID=

# ── spend cap (hosted deployments) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The daily ceiling on OpenAI spend, in dollars. Defaults to 10 when unset.
# Set it to what you can afford to lose in a day, because a determined caller
# can burn the whole day's budget: the extension needs no sign-in, so an
# anonymous caller has no identity we control. An explicit 0 turns the ceiling
# OFF -- leaving this line EMPTY does not, it falls back to the default.
# TRACELY_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=10
#
# Number of proxies YOU control in front of this server, counted from the right
# of X-Forwarded-For. Unset means the header is ignored entirely, which is
# correct for a direct connection -- a client sets that header itself, so
# trusting it would let anyone mint a fresh rate-limit key per request. Set to
# 1 behind a single reverse proxy (the hosted box has Apache in front).
# TRACELY_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1
#
# The test extension's Pro grant (see DEPLOY.md, "The test extension"). A
# caller sending X-Tracely-Beta with one of these comma-separated tokens is
# served as Pro on the extension's routes, on its own daily pool; empty or
# unset means beta is OFF. The pool's ceiling follows the rules above: empty
# is the default (10), an explicit 0 removes the ceiling -- it does not turn
# beta off. Both are re-read per request.
# TRACELY_BETA_TOKENS=
# TRACELY_BETA_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=10
#
# Student and Pro accounts' calls on the extension's routes spend a pool of
# their own, so the thorough model can never empty the day free users run on.
# When it is spent they run the fast model on the pool above. Same rules.
# TRACELY_PAID_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=10
#
# The desktop app routes' own pool (__global_app__). Same rules. When it is
# spent the app routes answer 503 and the extension's pools are untouched.
# TRACELY_APP_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=10
#
# Where the SQLite database lives. Defaults to ./data next to the server.
# MUST be a real process environment variable, NOT a line in this file:
# lib/db.js opens the database at ESM import time, which happens before
# server.js gets as far as reading .env. Set it in the systemd unit
# (Environment=TRACELY_DATA_DIR=...) or export it before launching.

# PORT=4477
# TRACELY_MOCK=1            # keyless mock mode for UI development
